# ${MODULE_NAME}

A Kobweb worker, which runs code in the background of a site
(see https://kobweb.varabyte.com/docs/concepts/foundation/workers).

Its logic goes in `src/jsMain/kotlin/${PACKAGE_PATH}/${NAME}WorkerFactory.kt`.
Kobweb generates the `${NAME}Worker` class from it.

To use the worker from a Kobweb application, add it to the application's dependencies:

```kotlin
jsMain.dependencies {
    implementation(project("${GRADLE_PATH}"))
}
```

Then create it in a composable and send it input:

```kotlin
val worker = rememberWorker { ${NAME}Worker { output -> println(output) } }
LaunchedEffect(Unit) {
    worker.postInput(${INPUT_EXAMPLE})
}
```
